required_changes.change:
Style the fold row's "Theme" as a section title:

details.hw-look-fold > summary.hw-look-name .hw-label { color: var(--hw-text); font-size: 13px; font-weight: 600; }

Or give the span class hw-sec-title instead. Either way keep id="theme-label", which the radiogroup's aria-labelledby uses.

Give the mini chip the grid chip's anatomy, 6 px shorter:

#theme-mini .hw-theme-face { height: 24px; min-width: 72px; padding: 0 8px 4px; }
#theme-mini .hw-theme-spark { left: 8px; right: 8px; bottom: 2px; }
@media (max-width: 199px) { #theme-mini .hw-theme-face { min-width: 64px; padding: 0 4px 4px; } }

Keep the cloned word, the chain mark and the dashed frame in the palette's label color. Never add the selection ring.

Use one section-row height, and put the marker beside the title:

details.hw-look-fold > summary.hw-look-name { min-height: var(--hw-row-h); padding: 3px var(--hw-gutter) 3px 28px; }
details.hw-look-fold > summary.hw-look-name::before { top: 10px; }

The 24 px chip from VT03 fits the 30 px row with 3 px to spare above and below.

Keep Change outside the fold row's box and align it:

details.hw-look-fold[open] > summary.hw-look-name { margin-right: 56px; padding-right: 0; }
details.hw-look-fold .hw-look-change { top: 2.6px; right: calc(var(--hw-gutter) - 2px); }

Zoomed layout (under 300 px): row 1 holds the title (plus the chip when folded) beside Change, and the line wraps under them at full width.

@media (max-width: 299px) {
  details.hw-look-fold > summary.hw-look-name, details.hw-look-fold[open] > summary.hw-look-name { display: grid; grid-template-areas: none; grid-template-columns: auto minmax(0,1fr); grid-template-rows: 24px; grid-auto-rows: auto; column-gap: 8px; row-gap: 2px; align-items: center; margin-right: 0; padding-right: var(--hw-gutter); }
  .hw-label { grid-area: 1 / 1; }
  .hw-look-mini { grid-area: 1 / 2; justify-self: start; }
  .hw-look-current { grid-area: 2 / 1 / 3 / -1; min-height: 2lh; }
  folded: .hw-look-current { min-height: 0; }
}

The last three selectors are scoped under details.hw-look-fold > summary.hw-look-name, as in proto-V.css.

Use one 8 px step after the title, and give the empty chip slot no gap:

details.hw-look-fold > summary.hw-look-name { column-gap: var(--hw-s2); }
details.hw-look-fold.hw-mini-none > summary.hw-look-name .hw-look-mini { display: none; }
